  "id": "08f3b322-5f43-52c3-b6ac-0c95e9bddd96",
  "slug": "air-fryer-puff-pastry-churros-recipe-11959195",
  "name": "Air Fryer Puff Pastry Churros",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "These air fryer puff pastry churros are a quick and irresistible twist on the classic treat\u2014crispy, golden, and coated in sweet cinnamon sugar, all without the hassle of deep frying. Made with store-bought puff pastry keeps things simple. Serve with nutella or strawberry topping for dipping.",
  "cuisine": "Mexican",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Line an air fryer basket with parchment paper cut down to the size of the bottom of the basket. Preheat the airfryer to 400 degrees F (200 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Roll out puff pastry on a slightly floured surface with a rolling pin. Cut into 12 3-inch strips with a pizza cutter."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Lay 6 strips of puff pastry spaced out into the air fryer and cook until golden brown, flipping half way through, for 6 to 8 minutes. Place pastry strips on a paper towel lined plate and set aside. Repeat with remaining puff pastry strips"
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Meanwhile, combine sugar and cinnamon in a large resealable bag and mix well. Add 6 churros to the bag with cinnamon sugar, seal and gently toss until well coated."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Enjoy as is or serve with with strawberry topping or nutella for dipping."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 6,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 6,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 10,
